Package: backtrack
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, borgbackup (>= 1.2)
Recommends: gvfs-backends, gvfs-fuse
Suggests: backtrack-nautilus, backtrack-dolphin
Description: browse your files as they were
 Backtrack keeps your files backed up and lets you move back through time to
 bring back what you lost. Pick a folder, step back to this morning or last
 week, and restore a file without needing to know how backups work. It is
 built on Borg Backup.

Package: backtrack-nautilus
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, backtrack (>= ${source:Version}), python3-nautilus
Description: Restore Previous Version in GNOME Files, for Backtrack
 Adds Restore Previous Version and Browse Backups of This Folder to GNOME
 Files, opening Backtrack at the file or folder.

Package: backtrack-dolphin
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, backtrack (>= ${source:Version}), dolphin
Description: Restore Previous Version in Dolphin, for Backtrack
 Adds Restore Previous Version and Browse Backups of This Folder to Dolphin,
 opening Backtrack at the file or folder.
